# **THE HEART OF AFRICA BEATS AT QPAC**

[![Mother Africa](/media/2014/03/STS_1080x1350-2-Version-2.jpg)](/media/2014/03/STS_1080x1350-2-Version-2.jpg)

After selling out in all capital cities across Australia in 2010 and smashing box office records, the jaw-dropping show _Mother Africa, Circus of the Senses_ returns to Brisbane, direct from a sell out Broadway season,to the **Playhouse**, **Queensland Performing Arts Centre** (**QPAC**) from **13 to 17 May 2014**.

 The heartbeat of Africa pulsates throughout the show, featuring new acts, new music and new costumes. Watch in awe as the musicians and artists articulate their passion and love for their homeland. This entertainment extravaganza combines the talents from nine African countries, including Ethiopia, South Africa, Kenya, Tanzania, Ivory Coast, Benin, Zimbabwe and Guinea, showcasing the wonder, suspense and joy of _Mother Africa_. Seen by over two million people worldwide _Mother Africa_ is a delight for the senses with bodies contorted into mind-boggling shapes and astonishing acrobatics, feel the rhythm as percussionists beat up a storm of sound and traditional dancers tell their own stories. Audiences will be overwhelmed by the complexity and versatility of these world-class acts. _Mother Africa_ is not just a traditional African show; it also has a take on the modern, dynamic culture of the new Africa. This is afresh and fantastic show that evokes passion and demands a response, do not miss out on seeing the amazing sets and costumes that bring forth the feel of authentic African traditions in _Mother Africa_.

_Physically compelling._ **Courier Mail**

_It’s the Lion king on steroids._ **Dominion Post, NZ**

_Mother Africa is exuberant, high-energy entertainment._ **New York Times**

_Rich in rhythm and robust in song, MOTHER AFRICA's acrobats, musicians and dancers light up the stage in a powerful performance of stunning African artistry._ **Theatre Mania, New York.**

_This jubilant 90-minute spectacle delivers one thrill after another._ **Time Out Magazine, New York**

_Spectacular and colourful - in the tradition of outstanding cirque performances...show of the year._ **Timeout Magazine, UK**

_A swirl of colour and movement that keeps its audience clapping and cheering throughout...Mother Africa is a vibrant high-energy production._

**The Gold Coast Bulletin**

_It’s Cirque Du Soleil with an abundant African flavour._ **Australian Stage**

_Pure spectacle, colourful costumes, immense physicality, powerfully rhythmic music, song, dance, cirque acts and comedy, something for everybody._ **Glam Adelaide**

  Rokitz Entertainment, Nue Levo and FKP Scorpio Present **Mother Africa**

**When:** 13 to 17 May 2014 **Where:** Playhouse, QPAC, Cultural Precinct, South Bank, Brisbane **Tickets\*:** Refer to [qpac.com.au](http://www.qpac.com.au/) for current pricing **Bookings:** [qpac.com.au](http://www.qpac.com.au/) or 136 246

